            <ArticleTitle>Morbid obesity and psoriasis: Disease remission after laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>370-372</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1871-403X(17)30030-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.orcp.2017.04.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Psoriasis is more frequent and severe in populations with obesity, and both have been associated with a higher cardiovascular risk. Recent studies suggest that weight loss may improve psoriasis and metabolic comorbidities in individuals with obesity. We present a case of a female patient affected by psoriasis, morbid obesity and other metabolic comorbidities, who experienced dramatic improvement in skin and joint symptoms and metabolic parameters after weight loss surgery with sleeve gastrectomy.</AbstractText>
